      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0121",
      "sequence": 976,
      "meaning": "The Lord instructs Hanumān to assume the form of a young brahmin, go to Ayodhyā, announce Rāma’s welfare to Bharata and return with news. The son of the Wind departs at once, while Rāma visits Bharadvāja. The sage worships him in many ways, offers praise and blessings, and the Lord bows at his feet before reboarding the aircraft. Guha hears of Rāma’s arrival and calls every boatman and boat; after the aircraft crosses the Gaṅgā it lands on the bank at Rāma’s command. Sītā worships and repeatedly bows to the river, who joyfully blesses her with unbroken married felicity. Guha runs near overcome by love; seeing Rāma with Vaidehī, he falls unconscious upon the ground. Delighted by his supreme love, Raghurāya raises him and embraces him to his heart.",
